No licence has been granted yet.

This repository contains the DashCue project. The project owner has not chosen a
licence, so no rights are granted by default: all rights are reserved, and the code,
documentation and artwork may not be redistributed or used commercially without the
owner's written permission.

This is a placeholder for a decision, not a licence. It exists because:

  * section 18 of the specification requires a LICENSE file in the repository root;
  * section 7.4 requires third-party licences to be tracked (see docs/LICENSES.md);
  * nothing in the specification chooses a licence for the project itself (see
    docs/SPEC_ISSUES.md, SI-07).

Before any public release, the owner must pick a licence. The choice is constrained by
what the project redistributes:

  * the UI font is planned to be Inter under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, which
    requires the font's licence to travel with it;
  * the brand artwork in branding/ is original to this project;
  * the firmware links an LGPL-2.1 Arduino core, which has its own obligations and is
    documented in docs/LICENSES.md.

See docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md section 0 for the outstanding decision.
